  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting livestock assets &amp; safeguarding livelihoods in Djibouti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food security assistance to vulnerable communities affected by drought in the Ali Sabeh, Dilkhil, Arta, Obock, Tadjourah regions. This FAO project safeguards livestock-based livelihoods and improve lives by treating and vaccinating livestock of affected households. The project also provides seeds to households ahead of the next agricultural season. FAO targets a total of 41,250 people, including 12,995 women, 12,500 men, 15,755 children, and 4,125 people with disabilities with this project.</narrative>
  </description>
